<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:49:11 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>Macron to meet new UK PM Burnham against backdrop of Bayeux Tapestry</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-macron-to-meet-new-uk-pm-burnham-against-backdrop-of-bayeux-tapestry</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron will travel to London on Wednesday for his first meeting with the United Kingdom's new prime minister, Andy Burnham, in what will be the first visit by a European Union leader since he took office. Macron will also unveil the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum in a "significant moment" for Franco-British relations. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5cad6ee0-a2d9-11f1-9f07-57f96fb022cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:47:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d03d4b4c-60a3-11f0-bc9e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-66AF26N.jpg">AFP - GONZALO FUENTES</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French presidential hopefuls clash over economy and EU in first debate</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-french-presidential-hopefuls-clash-over-economy-and-eu-in-first-debate</link><description>
Seven leading candidates in the race to succeed President Emmanuel Macron have clashed in their first debate ahead of the 2027 election, exposing sharp differences over the economy, public debt and France's relationship with the European Union.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">872c426c-a2c6-11f1-82aa-99d519c5795b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:07:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/309dabde-a2c6-11f1-ad7b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-27T162935Z-59374920-RC227NATGZTL-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-BUSINESS.jpg">REUTERS - Stephanie Lecocq</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French Foreign Legion soldier kidnapped by Colombian guerrilla faction</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260828-french-foreign-legion-soldier-kidnapped-in-southwestern-colombia-guerilla</link><description>
The Colombian army has announced that a soldier in the French Foreign Legion was kidnapped earlier this month while travelling through Narino, a region in southwestern Colombia dominated by guerrillas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21af97f2-a2a5-11f1-acd2-a97c7d4b6ac3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 06:49:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/560a40de-1f61-11ef-99d1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000_34U984T.jpg">AFP - DELPHINE MAYEUR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French sailors ditch GPS to rediscover celestial art of navigation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-looking-up-french-sailors-ditch-gps-to-rediscover-celestial-art-of-navigation</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the fourth of a five-part series, RFI meets amateur sailors learning to navigate by the stars, using a technique that allows them to find their position without GPS or onboard electronics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36764e-a1f5-11f1-b80f-89dd84255de2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:03:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4247340c-a151-11f1-9f33-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Margo-l-un-des-quatre-stagiaires-%C3%A0-bord-du-Whirlwind-s-exerce-%C3%A0-la-manipulation-du-sextant.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Former model sues French state over delay in Epstein recruiter rape investigation</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-former-model-sues-french-state-over-delay-in-epstein-recruiter-rape-investigation</link><description>
A former model who accused an alleged recruiter for American sex offender Jeffrey Epstein of raping her in the 1990s is suing the French state for delays to the investigation. The state is also being sued by a child protection organisation, on behalf of alleged Epstein victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25d4ac50-a214-11f1-8343-418826f8ad24</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:03:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fd9e7c3a-a190-11f1-b354-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A3WX7QX.jpg">© Joel Saget/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France to tie African development aid to efforts to limit migration to Mayotte</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-france-to-tie-african-development-aid-to-efforts-to-limit-migration-to-mayotte</link><description>
France plans to make its development aid to seven African countries conditional on greater cooperation in the fight against illegal immigration to the French island territory of Mayotte, as the issue becomes increasingly politicised ahead of the French presidential election next year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa5d8488-a200-11f1-b7e4-dd9f6f304afc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:30:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98391ee4-a15a-11f1-ac0e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6866ZR.jpg">© Marine Gachet/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French collector gathers lunar photos that changed our view of space</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-looking-up-french-collector-gathers-lunar-photos-that-changed-our-view-of-space</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the last of a five-part series, space historian and collector Victor Martin-Malburet talks to RFI about his passion for Nasa's Moon missions and the photos they produced. He began searching around the world for original prints aged 15 and has now amassed a collection of 1,500 photographs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/198dc942-a096-11f1-8aca-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0325.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/198dc942-a096-11f1-8aca-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0325.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7791844a-a08a-11f1-beed-d7a62653df5f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:11:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/198dc942-a096-11f1-8aca-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0325.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Second person dies after man deliberately drives into crowd in Caen</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-second-person-dies-after-man-deliberately-drives-into-crowd-in-caen</link><description>
A second person has died after a man deliberately drove his car into a group of people in the northern French city of Caen on Wednesday, leaving nine others injured.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f623464-a1f8-11f1-864a-d35118897ed7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:06:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4f546802-a1fd-11f1-b51b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6L439E.jpg">AFP - MATTHIEU CLAVEL</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France relaxes rules for three famous cheeses after summer drought</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-france-relaxes-rules-for-three-famous-cheeses-after-summer-drought</link><description>
The drought in France is forcing farmers who produce milk for some of the country's most famous cheeses to feed their cows differently, as scorched pastures make it increasingly difficult to stick to strict rules on protected regional foods, known as AOP. Temporary exemptions on fodder sources will apply to the producers of Abondance, Beaufort and Comté to cope with the grass shortage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bda251f2-a162-11f1-a385-89f34329e939</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 05:16:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg">© Wikipédia</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French soldiers disciplined over Rhodesian flags linked to white supremacists</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-soldiers-disciplined-over-rhodesian-flags-linked-to-white-supremacists</link><description>
France's Ministry of the Armed Forces has launched disciplinary proceedings against several soldiers photographed holding flags linked to Rhodesia, a former white minority-ruled territory in southern Africa whose symbols have been embraced by white supremacists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be541b62-a162-11f1-b918-37f5a52cec0d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French prosecutors investigate left-wing mayor over alleged misuse of public funds</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-prosecutors-investigate-leftwing-mayor-bagayoko-over-alleged-public-funds-misuse-ratp</link><description>
French financial prosecutors have opened an investigation into Bally Bagoyoko, the mayor of Saint-Denis, over suspected misuse of public funds during his employment by the Paris public transport operator RATP when he was also serving as a local elected official with the France Unbowed party. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">307bd96a-a135-11f1-ac41-09b89e57a360</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:50:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg">© Thomas Padilla / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: Amateur meteorite hunters search for clues to origins of universe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-looking-up-amateur-meteorite-hunters-search-for-clues-to-origins-of-universe</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the third of a five-part series, RFI hears from volunteers in south-west France who are searching for meteorites as part of a citizen science project designed to help researchers recover fragments from space.
