Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu arrives in the French overseas territory of Mayotte on Wednesday to try to speed up the reconstruction of the archipelago, 18 months after Cyclone Chido caused widespread destruction.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efd8954-a12d-11f1-9d4b-c95053c4254a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:46:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg">© PATRICK MEINHARDT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French radio enthusiast captures ISS signals from his garage</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-looking-up-french-radio-enthusiast-captures-iss-signals-from-his-garage</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the second episode of a five-part series, RFI hears from Vincent Plousey, a radio ham from Tavaux in eastern France whose hobby is picking up signals from the ISS using homemade antennas built in his garage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dd209ca-9fc0-11f1-b750-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:48:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French village reels from tornado that damaged hundreds of homes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-village-reels-from-tornado-that-damaged-hundreds-of-homes</link><description>
Hundreds of damaged homes, widespread power cuts and blocked roads confronted residents of southwestern France on Tuesday after a tornado tore through the village of Pomas, injuring 39 people, two of them critically.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36d51c-a04c-11f1-93b2-dd9b3ccbcf49</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:59:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg">AFP - CYRILLE KALDOR / UGC / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Sophie Adenot returns to the void for second spacewalk in a week</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-to-make-second-spacewalk-to-finish-repairs</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot on Tuesday stepped outside the International Space Station (ISS) for the second time, a week after she became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Adenot and US astronaut Anil Menon are due to finish replacing a faulty antenna on the ISS after running out of time during their first spacewalk on 18 August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d50039fa-9fc2-11f1-b33b-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg">via REUTERS - NASA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Centre-left Glucksmann enters French presidential race as left tries to unite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260824-centre-left-glucksmann-enters-french-presidential-race-as-left-tries-to-unite</link><description>
French centre-left politician Raphael Glucksmann has announced his candidacy for next year's presidential election, seeking to challenge hard-left leader Jean-Luc Melenchon to lead France's fractured left, as a campaign increasingly dominated by the far right takes shape.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4365a168-9f83-11f1-8a80-dd78f7da95c3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:18:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Scorching summer takes toll on bees and honey harvests in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-scorching-summer-takes-toll-on-bees-and-honey-harvests-in-france</link><description>
France produces 20,000 tonnes of honey each year, but successive heatwaves and persistent drought across Europe this summer are impacting bee populations as flowering plants dry out and colonies struggle to find food. Beekeeper Romain Lacotte and his family farm 1,000 hives in Haute-Corrèze, central France, an area considered one of the country's natural water towers. But even there, he tells RFI, high temperatures and lack of rain are taking their toll.
